<title>DENMARK: Tele Denmark rises on BT stake rumour. [CORRECTED 13:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>Tele Denmark rises on BT stake rumour. [CORRECTED 13:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish telecoms group Tele Danmark's share rose four percent on Wednesday on market rumours that British giant BT intended to take a stake in the 51 percent state-owned Danish firm.</p>
<p>At 1300 GMT the share stood at 333.00 crowns, up 12 crowns from Tuesday's close.</p>
<p>Both companies, which together with Norway's Telenor are equal partners in Swedish joint-venture Telenordia (corrects name of Swedish joint venture from 'Telenor' to 'Telenordia'), declined to comment on the rumours. </p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
